<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to buy 28,000/T Sept N+A naphtha.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to buy 28,000/T Sept N+A naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to buy 28,000 tonnes of naphthenic-and-aromatic (N+A) naphtha for September 11-20 delivery, a company offcial said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender which seeks the cargo on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis to Kaohsiung, closes July 31 and is valid for one day.</p>
<p>CPC's last N+A purchase, for August 15-31 delivery, was above $195 per tonne, c-and-f.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
